# Spec 06 Phase B — Derived supplies kit + concierge order (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before build)
# B1 GIVEN scanned inventory cube and item mix, WHEN KitEstimator runs, THEN it
#    returns small/medium/large boxes plus wardrobe, dishPack, tape, paper, wrap,
#    and mattressBags using centralized LOCKED-pending-calibration constants.
# B2 GIVEN boxable inventory, WHEN quantities are estimated, THEN the size-bucket
#    raw box demand receives exactly 12% headroom before each count rounds up.
# B3 GIVEN beds and hanging-clothes counts, WHEN a kit is estimated, THEN
#    mattressBags equals bed count and wardrobe boxes equal hanging capacity rounded up.
# B4 GIVEN first packing-plan creation, WHEN persistence completes, THEN exactly one
#    PACKING_SUPPLIES_KIT in-app task exists with an itemized kit, one placeholder
#    price, disclosed locked headroom copy, and a delivery date before session one.
# B5 GIVEN the kit view, WHEN Customize is used, THEN its single quantity sheet saves
#    all editable counts and recomputes the price; WHEN No thanks is used, THEN the
#    task leaves Home permanently but remains reopenable in the Tasks tab.
# B6 GIVEN an unsubscribed user, WHEN Order my kit is tapped, THEN the existing hard
#    paywall gate renders; after entitlement, submission uses workflowId supplies_kit
#    and persists a complete kit + authoritative identity payload.
# B7 GIVEN a supplies_kit submission, WHEN submitWorkflowAnswers handles it, THEN the
#    PACKING_SUPPLIES_KIT task enters matching_in_progress and direct best-effort SMS
#    uses the approved `PEEZY KIT ORDER: ...` family or logs `SMS notify not configured`.
# B8 GIVEN the sanctioned catalog reseed, WHEN it completes, THEN
#    BUY_PACKING_SUPPLIES is absent, the live catalog count matches JSON, and no ghosts exist.
# B9 GIVEN the Phase B diff and deployed sanctioned surfaces, WHEN a fresh-context
#    validator runs estimator tests plus the live iPhone/Firestore/function acceptance,
#    THEN every B criterion receives PASS/FAIL with evidence.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - The 12% headroom applies to raw small/medium/large box demand. Exact-fit accessories
#   (one mattress bag per bed, wardrobe capacity, one dish pack when kitchen items exist)
#   are not doubled by rounding 1.12 units to 2; tape/paper/wrap derive from headed boxes.
# - `No thanks` means permanently dismissed from Home, not deleted: store UserInProgress
#   with no return date so the stable task remains an explicit Tasks-tab escape hatch.
# - Until a supplier signs, centralized retail placeholders produce an `Estimated kit`
#   price line. No vendor promise, cart handoff, or fulfillment integration is inferred.
# - WorkflowService keeps its deployed answer envelope: complete kit and identity objects
#   are losslessly JSON-encoded into named answer rows, matching the approved mover payload.
#
